statement:
Two accounts, each with its own mutex. Two functions move money between them:

```cpp
struct Account { std::mutex m; long balance; };
Account alice, bob;
```

This runs fine for weeks and then hangs under load, with two threads stuck and no CPU being used. **Click the line that makes the deadlock possible.**

payload.code:
void alice_pays_bob(long amount) {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> la(alice.m);
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lb(bob.m);
    alice.balance -= amount;
    bob.balance   += amount;
}

void bob_pays_alice(long amount) {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lb(bob.m);
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> la(alice.m);
    bob.balance   -= amount;
    alice.balance += amount;
}
